[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

[b]Every town has a board with the mercenary contracts on offer.[/b]

Which kingdoms would hire you, what they pay and who they are fighting, on one page. It is only a view of vanilla's own offers: the same conditions and the same pay a lord would give you in conversation, and signing or switching uses vanilla's own actions.

[h1]The board[/h1]
In any town menu, pick [b]Mercenary Contract Board[/b]. Every kingdom is listed with its banner and its pay per influence point. Hover a line for the ruler, what signing is worth and the kingdom's wars. Kingdoms that won't hire you are greyed, with the reason. Pick one and press Accept.

[h1]Already under contract?[/h1]
[list]
[*]Your contract is at the top: the kingdom, its pay, the next monthly pay review, the influence still owed to you, its wars.
[*]Accepting another contract asks first: [i]"Leave your contract with Vlandia and sign with Battania?"[/i] Yes switches, No takes you back.
[*]Vassals and rulers get no contracts, and the board says so.
[/list]

[h1]Vanilla's rules, in plain view[/h1]
[list]
[*]Only kingdoms at war hire mercenaries.
[*]Clan tier 1 or more, the ruler's relation at least -10, no settlement of your own, and your wars must be theirs too.
[*]They must have heard of you, and not be winning on their own.
[*]Pay is denars per influence point you earn in their service, 10 to 800, higher when the kingdom is struggling.
[/list]

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Settings in Mod Configuration Menu (optional): enabled, show kingdoms that would not hire you, best pay first, confirm a first contract.
[*]No Harmony needed. Towns only (port towns too). English only for now.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[/list]
Works with or without War Sails. For Bannerlord v1.4.8. Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
